markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Reflection

Take a moment with this before revealing a way to think about it.

<details style="margin-top: 12px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;">
  <summary style="background-color: #E4E2F8; padding: 12px 16px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; font-size: 16px;">
    &#128161; Where do you expect your students to get stuck first: syntax, functions, or translating pseudocode to code?
  </summary>
  <div style="background-color: #FFFFFF; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #ACA8EA; font-size: 16px; color: #1A1A1A; line-height: 1.6;">
    There's no single right answer here, but each option has real evidence behind it from this lesson's own facilitation notes. Translating pseudocode into code asks students to turn a loose, informal strategy into something precise enough to trace by hand, that leap trips up students who skip steps that feel "too obvious" to write down. Syntax errors, missing quotes, forgetting the f-string's curly braces, show up immediately and are usually quick to fix once spotted. Return values tend to cause the most prolonged confusion of the three, since the mistake isn't a visible error message, it's a conceptual gap: a function can run successfully and still produce zero output, and that's genuinely counterintuitive the first time you see it.
  </div>
</details>

<hr>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 24px 0 16px 0;">
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
    <div style="background-color: #ACA8EA; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 20px; width: 36px; height: 36px; min-width: 36px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">&#10003;</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #1F1976;">
      <strong>Lesson 3 Complete</strong><br>
      Nice work! You've finished Python Basics.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 20px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <span style="font-size: 11pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; opacity: 0.8;">Up Next</span><br>
  <span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold;">Lesson 4: Optimization in Action</span>
</div>
MARKDOWN
